            0.188,
            0.517,
            0.383,
            0.539
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reading Fractions"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.185,
            0.548,
            0.873,
            0.658
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We usually read the fraction "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 3 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " as ‘three quarters’ or ‘three upon four’, but reading it as ‘3 times "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 4 } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " helps us to understand the size of the fraction because it clearly shows what the fractional unit is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( \\frac { 1 } { 4 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and how many such fractional units (3) there are."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.685,
            0.871,
            0.741
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Recall what we call the top number and the bottom number of fractions. In the fraction "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 5 } { 6 } , 5"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "numerator",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and 6 is the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "denominator.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.44,
            0.761,
            0.609,
            0.782
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Teacher’s Note"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.18,
            0.787,
            0.87,
            0.855
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Give several opportunities to the children to explore the idea of fractional units with different shapes like circles, squares, rectangles, triangles, etc."
            }
          ]
        },
